From: Armada contributors
Subject: [PATCH] cellular: serialize data toggles and discard removed modem state

Wait for profile updates before activation/disconnection. Coalesce overlapping
requests to the latest desired state and allow a never-used APN to be enabled.
Clear stale NM profiles when a device disappears and rebuild only valid modem
objects. Keep old QObject models alive until consumers have seen the new list.

diff --git a/libs/cellular/cellularmodem.cpp b/libs/cellular/cellularmodem.cpp
--- a/libs/cellular/cellularmodem.cpp
+++ b/libs/cellular/cellularmodem.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@ CellularModem::CellularModem(QObject *parent, ModemManager::ModemDevice::Ptr mmM
     connect(NetworkManager::notifier(), &NetworkManager::Notifier::activeConnectionRemoved, this, &CellularModem::mobileDataEnabledChanged);
     connect(NetworkManager::notifier(), &NetworkManager::Notifier::deviceAdded, this, &CellularModem::findNetworkManagerDevice);
     connect(NetworkManager::notifier(), &NetworkManager::Notifier::deviceRemoved, this, &CellularModem::findNetworkManagerDevice);
+    connect(NetworkManager::notifier(), &NetworkManager::Notifier::wwanEnabledChanged, this, &CellularModem::mobileDataEnabledChanged);
 
     // this is guaranteed to be a GSM modem
     m_mm3gppDevice = m_mmModem->interface(ModemManager::ModemDevice::GsmInterface).objectCast<ModemManager::Modem3gpp>();
@@ -77,6 +78,9 @@ CellularModem::CellularModem(QObject *parent, ModemManager::ModemDevice::Ptr mmM
 
